- Incorrect ledger transition.

### 18.2 Test quality standards

Tests must exercise actual production logic wherever feasible.

Avoid creating parallel test-only implementations of production behavior.

Use deterministic fixtures and stable assertions.

Avoid reliance on execution order.

Ensure test cleanup is safe.

Do not lower existing assertions or skip failing tests merely to make CI green.

Do not introduce meaningless coverage targets.

### 18.3 Regression control

Before changing a module:

1. Identify existing tests.
2. Record the baseline.
3. Introduce a failing regression test where practical.
4. Implement the smallest correct change.
5. Run focused tests.
6. Run relevant integration tests.
7. Run broader regression tests.
8. Inspect the final diff.

Any unavailable test must be reported as not executed.

